                    xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System">

    <!--
        iBarter English (default) UI strings.

        x:String is the XAML 2009 intrinsic type, so it resolves to
        System.String at BAML load time WITHOUT requiring an assembly
        reference.  The previous build of this file used
        xmlns:system="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib" + <system:String>,
        but `mscorlib` is .NET Framework only - on .NET 10 (Core) the
        assembly is renamed to System.Private.CoreLib, so the namespace
        declaration failed at runtime and every {DynamicResource str.X}
        lookup returned null (which is why every menu / button / label
        in the UI disappeared).

        Key convention:  str.<Area>.<SubArea>.<Key>  dot-separated.
        Areas (Phase 2): Menu / Dock / MainWindow / Splash / Banner /
                         Planner / Storage / Scanner / ShipCargo / Grid.<View>.

        Phase 2 adds the UI chrome (menus, docks, buttons, tooltips,
        column headers). Phase 3 fills Strings.zh-TW.xaml with real
        translations; Phase 5+ add tier/label/log strings.
    -->

